namespace eval pix::color {
    # Ruff documentation
    variable _ruff_preamble {
* The following color formats can be used:
rgba - e.g : *rgba(r,g,b,a)*<br>
This format takes four arguments: *red*, *green*, and *blue* as **integers**
between **0** and **255**, and *alpha* as a **floating-point** number between **0.0** and **1.0**.
hexHtml - e.g : *#F8D1DD*<br>
This format takes a single string argument representing a hexadecimal color code.
The hex code must be **7** characters long (including the '#' symbol), and each
subsequent character must be a valid hexadecimal digit.
rgb - e.g : *rgb(r,g,b)*<br>
This format takes three arguments for the *red*, *green*, and *blue*
components of the color. All arguments are **integer** numbers between **0** and **255**.
hexalpha - e.g : *FF0000FF*<br>
A string of **8** hexadecimal characters (case-insensitive), typically representing
an **RGBA** color format.
hex - e.g : *FF0000*<br>
A string of **6** hexadecimal characters (case-insensitive), typically representing
an **RGB** color format.
rgbx - e.g : *rgbx(r,g,b,x)*<br>
This format takes four arguments: *red*, *green*, *blue*, and *alpha* components.
Unlike standard rgba, all four arguments in this format are **integers** between **0** and **255**.
simple color - e.g : *{0.0 0.0 0.0 0.0}* or *{0.0 0.0 0.0}*<br>
This format takes a Tcl list of **three or four floating-point** numbers
between **0.0** and **1.0**, representing the *red*, *green*, *blue*, and optional *alpha* components.
string color - e.g : *white*<br>
A standard HTML or CSS color specified by its name.
hsv - e.g : *hsv(h,s,v)*<br>
This format takes three floating-point arguments for *hue* (**0 to 360**),
*saturation* (**0 to 100**), and *value* (**0 to 100**) components.
hsl - e.g : *hsl(h,s,l)*<br>
This format takes three floating-point arguments for *hue* (**0 to 360**),
*saturation* (**0 to 100**), and *lightness* (**0 to 100**) components.
tiny hex - e.g : *#FF6*<br>
A shorthand hexadecimal notation of **4** characters (including the '#' symbol),
where each color digit is automatically doubled (e.g., #RGB expands to #RRGGBB).
}
}
